            <ArticleTitle>Sponsored parachute jumps--can they cause prolonged pain?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>60-1</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A survey of parachute injuries sustained in 1984 at a local parachute club was made using hospital notes and a questionnaire. The overall injury rate was 0.2%. The injury rate in first time jumpers was 1.1%. The injuries often resulted in a prolonged hospital stay, time off work and residual pain and disability. Injury rates may be reduced by more prolonged and intensive training preceding the first jumps. Those people not interested in parachuting as a regular sport and who jump once only in order to raise money for charity are at risk of serious injury and perhaps should consider less dangerous alternatives.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
